REMARK 400 COMPOUND                                                             
REMARK 400 THIS MODEL IS THAT OF THE C319D MUTANT AT 2.0 ANGSTROMS.             
REMARK 400 THREE NONIDENTICAL CHAINS, GAMMA (A), BETA (B), AND ALPHA            
REMARK 400 (C) FORM ONE (ABC)-UNIT.  THE ASYMMETRIC UNIT CONTAINS ONE           
REMARK 400 (ABC)-UNIT.                                                          
REMARK 400 RESIDUES 317 - 331 OF THE MOBILE ACTIVE SITE FLAP IN CHAIN           
REMARK 400 C, BECOME SUFFICIENTLY DISORDERED THAT THEY ARE NOT                  
REMARK 400 MODELED.                                                             
REMARK 400 THREE WATERS, 500, 501, AND 502 ARE LIGATED TO THE ACTIVE            
REMARK 400 SITE NICKEL IONS.  THEY MUST BE PARTIALLY OCCUPIED DUE TO            
REMARK 400 CLOSE OXYGEN-OXYGEN DISTANCES BETWEEN THEM.                          
